# The script `mise run ffi-test` has the editor's headless mode run against
# the config in `config/`, of which it loads nothing: there is no `reload`.
# So every command it runs is one the editor ships, compiled in. What it
# prints must be exactly `evil-expected`.

# `i` begins an insert, and each key that prints is typed text. The scene
# shows the text, the bar after it, and the state's name first in the
# status line. The buffer is modified.
key i KeyI -
key h KeyH -
key e KeyE -
key l KeyL -
key l KeyL -
key o KeyO -
scene

# `<Escape>` returns to normal state: the cursor is on the last character
# typed, one cell back from the bar.
key <Escape> Escape -
scene

# `0` is a motion in normal state: the cursor goes to the line's start.
key 0 Digit0 -
scene
